^VERIFICATION
--
Today symbolic execution stops with "pointer handling for concurrency is
unsound" (goto_symex_state.cpp, #305) before any property is checked; the
test expects that message.  Once cbmc gets past it, update this desc: the
test is meant to check the _Lockit model, and with today's model (no
effect) assertion 1, "one index per id", is expected to FAIL (two threads
each assign a new index); with a model that excludes the second thread it
holds, and only "WRONG (must FAIL)" fails.  The program declares _Lockit and
_Id_cnt without defining them, as the MSVC STL's headers do (the runtime
defines them); g++ and clang++ accept it with those two definitions added.
